  "chapter": {
    "number": 132,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(133)",
          {
            "noteId": 239
          },
          "A Song of Degrees."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "See now! what is so good, or what so pleasant, as for brethren to dwell together?",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "It is as ointment on the head, that ran down to the beard, even the beard of Aaron; that ran down to the fringe of his clothing.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "As the dew of Aermon, that comes down on the mountains of Sion: for there, the Lord commanded the blessing, even life for ever.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
